---
const points = [
  {
    title: 'Six letters, one .com',
    body: 'waxphx is six characters. With the dot and com it is still easy to say, spell, and fit on an awning, an app icon, or an Instagram handle.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The TLD people trust',
    body: '.com is still the default people type when they half-remember a name. For a local service brand, that habit is worth more than a clever new extension.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Keywords without the stuffed URL',
    body: '“Wax” plus “PHX” reads instantly as waxing in Phoenix. It lines up with searches for body waxing, Brazilian waxing, and hair removal without looking like a keyword string.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A name you can defend',
    body: 'Geo-plus-service .coms in a large metro are scarce. Owning this one keeps a competitor from sitting on the obvious address while you build the brand on something weaker.',
  },
  {
    title: 'What it does for search — honestly',
    body: 'An exact .com helps recall, direct navigation, and the anchor text other sites use. It does not outrank a stronger site by magic. The buyer still has to publish, earn reviews, and show up on the map.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Ready for more than one studio',
    body: 'Use it as the flagship, then add a matching industry extension such as .salon if you want a second door. The .com stays the name people remember.',
  },
];
---

<section id="why" class="scroll-mt-24 border-b border-line bg-cream">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-clay">Why buyers want it</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">A practical name, not a slogan.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-mute">
        Premium here means short, obvious, and already in the category. The page does not invent a domain-authority score. Authority is earned with links after you own the name.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {
        points.map((point, index) => (
          <li class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-paper p-6">
            <p class="font-display text-2xl text-clay">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{point.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mute">{point.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
